WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.234
-October 11th is
National Coming Out Day,

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.771
when the LGBTQ community
celebrates

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.206
the brave act of coming out.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:08.775
But one thing the community
isn't celebrating lately

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.677
is the disappearance
of lesbian bars.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.578
According to
"Smithsonian" magazine,

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.314
there are only 15 left
in the whole country.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.149
One of our writers, Jenny Hagel,
is a lesbian

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.919
and she decided to investigate.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.989
[ Mid-tempo jazz plays ]

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:25.391
-Hey!
I'm Jenny Hagel,

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.692
and I'm here at
Henrietta Hudson,

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.961
New York's
longest-running lesbian bar.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.897
I'm going to talk to the owner,
Lisa Cannistraci --

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.198
-Hey, what's up?

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.000
-...about why our bars
are disappearing.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.669
But, first, because they're
disappearing so fast,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.671
before we talk,
I have to inspect the place

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.372
and make sure
it's still a lesbian bar.

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:41.508
Is that okay?
-Let's go.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.875
-Alright.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.211
Alright, let's see
what we got here.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.713
We got beer. Check.

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:49.815
Queer insignia. Check.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.851
Masculine light fixture.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.721
Sturdily built and
well-sanded bar. Check.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:59.458
Woman in an outfit that's
both stylish and comfortable.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.994
Yeah. This checks out.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.229
[ Sighs ] Okay?

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.798
Now that we have completed
our checklist

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:09.135
and established that this is,
in fact, a lesbian bar,

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.770
I want to ask you
a few questions.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.071
That alright?
-Sure. Let's do it.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.607
-So, tell me a little bit
about lesbian bars.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.709
What role have they played
in the queer community?

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.878
-Sure.
Lesbian bars, gay bars,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:23.049
queer bars, and those spaces
are a safe haven.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:26.252
I know I've seen young
queer people walk into here,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.789
into this space,
and they look around,

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.758
and it's their first time
in a queer bar.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.058
And they sit down,

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.594
and you just literally see
their shoulders go down.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:38.964
You see the exhale.
And you can just see

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:40.433
the transformation
right in front of you.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.334
It's beautiful.
-I remember going into --

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.170
the very first time I went
to a lesbian bar.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.072
And you don't realize
all the tiny ways

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.107
in which you adjust yourself,
as you walk through the world,

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.376
to try to fit in or
seem a little different.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.111
-Yeah.
-A little, like, straighter.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.580
A little more mainstream.
-Sure.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.648
-And I felt like I, like,
sat down at the bar.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.250
and all that washed off me.
And I was just --

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.018
-Yeah, yourself.
-My little gay self.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.720
-Yeah.
It was raining the other day,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.656
and I was walking with somebody,
and I put my umbrella up.

00:02:04.656 --> 00:02:07.459
And I said, you know --
because it was one umbrella.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.161
And I put my arm
around the person,

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:11.163
and I said,
"I remember, in the '80s,

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:13.098
it was the only time I could
put my arm around my girlfriend,

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:16.669
was when it was raining, because
you could get away with it.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.937
You know?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.338
-Here's
the million-dollar question.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.441
Why are lesbian bars
disappearing?

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:24.110
-Because lesbians can assimilate

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.011
much more easily
into mainstream society.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:28.581
For example, like, now they're
making out at Applebee's.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.718
They really don't need to come
to the West Village anymore.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.985
-They used to come here
to make out,

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:35.454
but now they can make out
at the food court.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.090
They're making out at Cinnabon.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.424
They're making out
at Orange Julius.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.592
-Something like that.
-Right?

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.127
They're making out
at Panda Express.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.195
-It's horrendous.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.030
And bad for business,
more importantly.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.500
For those who don't know, can
you tell me what nesting is?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.836
-So, nesting is
when two lesbians meet

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.539
and they hook up,
they make out at Applebee's,

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.774
and then they essentially
move in together,

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.676
and they stay home and
play Trivial Pursuit

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.545
and make pasta.
And it's very bad for business.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:00.579
We don't like that.
-You're describing

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:02.215
my ideal night.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.784
So I never introduce people to
each other, even if they beg me.

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:07.153
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.055
-So, once they start nesting,
they start staying home

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.489
and they don't come here
and spend their money.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.157
-It's not good.
But then, when they break up,

00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:14.160
they drink every night,
so it's not that bad.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.929
You know, it is a cycle.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.264
-When you first opened
Henrietta's,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.565
it was a lesbian bar.
-Sure.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.067
Is that still
how you refer to it,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.436
or has how you refer to the bar
evolved?

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.737
-It's evolved over the years.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.739
Now, as the community's
getting bigger

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.707
and people are, like,
really in tune

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:32.044
and can be more specific
about how they identify,

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.380
we refer to ourselves

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.016
as a queer human bar
built by lesbians.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.318
-That's great,
because nothing is stronger

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.752
than something
built by lesbians.

00:03:40.752 --> 00:03:42.888
-That's true. Yep.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.457
What's your favorite
pick-up line?

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.360
-"Oh, hey, can I have a kiss?"
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.996
That's very direct.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.064
It's actually worked a lot
in the '90s.

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:56.202
-So, I'm just going to write,
"Can I have a kiss?"

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.604
If you had to estimate --
the bar's been open 30 years --

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.807
how many breakups do you think
have happened

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:03.476
inside these walls?
-I've gotten a lot of

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.312
"thank yous" for relationships
that started here.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.446
-Aww, that's great.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.714
-With families
and stuff like that.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.816
I don't get a lot of e-mails
about the breakups.

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.652
-[ Laughs ]
They should be required.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.854
They should be required to
register their breakup with you.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.789
Well, Lisa, this has been great.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.091
So, now that you've helped me

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:21.927
understand some of the issues
going on around lesbian bars,

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:24.597
I want to see if I can help you.
Does that sound good?

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.998
-Sure.
-Great. Let's head to the bar.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.367
-Let's do it.
-Go ahead.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.768
-Okay, so, just to end
on a fun note,

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:33.272
I really want there to be more
lesbian bars in the world.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.908
So, just in case someone is
thinking about opening one,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.609
but they don't have,
like, the right name,

00:04:37.609 --> 00:04:40.513
I have come up with a few names
for lesbian bars.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.114
Just possible names.
And you're the expert.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.449
So I'm going to
show them to you,

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.284
and you tell me
if these are good names.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.052
-Let's do it.
-Queer Goggles.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:50.189
-Maybe in Britain.
-LGBTGI Fridays.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.091
-[ Chuckles ] Aah.
-No?

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.292
-Nah.
-It doesn't roll --

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.560
A little too clumsy
on the tongue?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.295
-You forgot the "Q."
-I did that.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.397
You're exactly right.
Okay, now this is, like,

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.666
for if you're going to open
in an Irish bar.

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.535
-Sure.
-Flannelgans.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.203
-Ooh, yes.
-Yes? Great.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.338
-Park Slope.
-Park Slope. Exactly.

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:07.607
Alright. Oh, man.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.541
Your Ex-Girlfriend is
Probably in Here.

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:11.610
-I think that's
the name of this place.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.512
-It probably is
the name of this place?

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:16.015
-Yeah, in parentheses, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.216
Lady Cheers.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.284
It's like Cheers,
but for ladies.

00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:20.987
-Not feeling it.
-Not feeling it?

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.321
-Nah.
-Alright. You know what?

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.690
I'll meet you at Flannelgans.
-Absolutely. Let's do it.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.259
-[ Laughs ]
-Pitchers.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.561
-Alright, so, Lisa,
you just renovated your bar

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.962
and reopened it.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.930
And I want the relaunch
to go great.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.634
So I've come up with
a few drink specials

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.468
that I think you could offer
to drum up business.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:37.903
So I'm just gonna
show them to you.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.138
And then you tell me
what you think of them, okay?

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.206
-Sure.
-Okay.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:43.343
-Let's do it.
-Alright. The Cartini.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.145
It's a martini
served in a glass Subaru.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.614
Like, it's sporty, but
it will get you drunk.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.182
-I'm thinking -- Yeah, as a --

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:54.153
maybe a big one in, like,
a sharing, like a bowl.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.521
-Great.
-Yeah, I'm in.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.924
-Yeah? Good.
This is the First Date.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.926
It's a bourbon and a lease.
-Ooh.

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:02.895
That would go over very well.
-Right?

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.030
-Yes.
-Alright.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.365
And finally,
the Tegan and Sara.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.468
it's just two identical drinks.
-Love it.

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:09.669
-Yeah?
-You know why?

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:10.803
-Why?

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.205
-You get to ring up
two drinks at once.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.039
-There you go.
See, this is your profit margin.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:16.041
-We're putting that on the menu
immediately.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.377
-Great. Alright.
-I love it. That's great.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.779
-I'm in. Can I --

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.947
I think -- Did I just get hired
as a bartender?

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.384
-Um, sure, as a fill-in.
-A fill-in. Okay, right.

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:25.917
I have to work my way up.
I understand.

00:06:25.917 --> 00:06:27.420
Okay, that's fair.
-Fantastic.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.621
-Great.
-You're in.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.456
-Hey, thank you so much
for talking to me today.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.791
I really appreciate it.
And if you live

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:35.127
near a lesbian bar,
please consider supporting it.

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:37.262
And if you don't live
near a lesbian bar,

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:39.498
consider opening one,
and letting me and Lisa

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:40.966
drink there for free.
-Yes.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:43.736
Thank you.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:47.139
-Jenny Hagel, everybody.
And thanks to Lisa Cannistraci

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.409
at Henrietta Hudson
for welcoming us into her bar.

